{#- Guidance Layer -#}
Only generate character arc fragments. Do not add new characters, do not repeat complete profiles.

## Output Field Description
- `character_arcs`: List of character arcs, each containing `name` (verbatim from fixed character roster) and `arc` (transformation arc from start to end, including stages, psychological changes, emotional changes, and chapter clues).

## Pipeline Boundary
This template is only for splitting the final arc fragment of the character generation pipeline.
It can only write or correct `arc` for existing profiles, cannot create new characters, cannot output complete `character_bible`, and cannot rewrite relationship matrix.
Character arcs should be independently generated at this stage according to the field contract, without using other templates for remediation.

## Canonical name / Chapter Boundary Rules
- `name` can only come from roster canonical name; aliases, old names, past-life names, or misnomers can only appear as brief explanations in the `arc` string.
- Arcs can describe chapter stages, but early reveals cannot be written as early confirmations; chapter boundaries must be left to NarrativeContract / ChapterContractIndex management.
- Do not copy character encyclopedia entries; only write start point, pressure, choice cost, stage transformation, and end direction.

